# E030: DuplicateKey at eval time — two different EscapedRef keys resolve to the same string.
# The parser cannot catch this because $k1 and $k2 have different names.
# Keys in the inner dict are evaluated in the outer dict's scope (parent_env rule),
# so $k1 and $k2 both resolve to "x", triggering a runtime duplicate-key error.
[k1: "x"  k2: "x"  result: [$k1: 1  $k2: 2]]
=== error
[E030] duplicate key: <computed key> (defined at 4:37-4:43)
